# Mini Template

A small, dependency-free TypeScript template renderer for Bun.

```ts
import { render } from "./src/engine";

render("Hello, {{user.name}}!", { user: { name: "Ada" } });
```

`{{value}}` HTML-escapes text, while `{{{value}}}` emits raw text. The renderer
also supports nested `{{#if path}}...{{else}}...{{/if}}` and
`{{#each path}}...{{else}}...{{/each}}` blocks, comments (`{{! ... }}`), and
`{{this}}` / `{{@index}}` inside loops. Loop paths first use the current item
and then fall back to the root data object.

Run from the command line:

```sh
bun run src/cli.ts template.txt data.json
```

The rendered text is the only stdout output. Parse, file, and template errors
are written to stderr and return a non-zero exit status.

Run the tests with `bun test`.

